  "strategy": "Approach and rationale\nThe central idea is to represent the step function h(x) using a compact basis expansion in a smooth space, then optimize over those coefficients. This differs from discrete optimization by allowing smoother transitions and leveraging mathematical analytic tools. The basis expansion captures global structure while maintaining integrability and continuity. The basis spans L2 rather than being discrete, enabling more effective optimization techniques. The key advantage is that gradients can be computed more readily and meaningful constraints on coefficients can be imposed. This approach should overcome local optima in discrete spaces by exploring continuous landscapes.\n\nMathematical specification\nVariables: \n- Basis coefficients \u03b8 in \u211d^p (p small)\n- Integration domain [0,2]\n- Constraint: \u222bh(x)dx=1\n- Corruption: \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx for k\u2208[-n+1, n-1]\n\nRepresentation:\nh(x) = \u03a3_{k=1}^{p} x_k \u03c6_k(x) + \u03bc, \nwhere \u03c6_k are chosen basis functions (with \u03c6_k orthogonal under dx measure), and \u03bc is a constant.\n\nConstraints:\n0 \u2264 \u03a3_{k=1}^{p} x_k \u03c6_k(x) + \u03bc \u2264 1, \u2200x\u2208[0,2]\n\u222bh(x)dx =1\n\nVariables: \u03b8 = [x_1, ..., x_p, \u03bc]^T \u2208 \u211d^{p+1}\n\nObjective: \nmin \u03b8 max_k \u222bh(x)[1-h(x+k)]dx\n\nSmooth version:\nC_smooth(\u03b8) = (1/\u03b1) log(\u03a3exp(\u03b1 \u222bh[1-h(\u00b7+k)]dx))\n\nImplementation procedure\n1. Initialization:\n- Load parent solution h_parent (n=500)\n- Project h_parent to continuous space using SVD truncation\n- Use projected gradient ascent to find initial basis and coefficients\n\n2. Optimization Problem:\n- Variables: \u03b8\n- Objective: Smooth max correlated coefficient\n- Constraints: [0,1] bounds and integral constraint\n- Method: Projected gradient with barrier function\n\n3. Formulation:\n- Basis selection: Trigonometric basis for [0,2] interval \n- Cost function using log-sum-exp smoothing\n- Barrier parameters: \u21131-norm barrier for coefficients \n\n4. Iterative Update:\nFor each iteration:\na) Compute h(x) at all points\nb) Evaluate barrier violations\nc) Compute gradient including penalty\nd) Update coefficients with SGDS\ne) Project to feasible space\n\n5. Termination:\n- Max iterations 10\u2074\n- Residual norm < 1e\u207b\u2077\n- No improvement in 100 steps\n\nSearch choices and useful variations\n- Basis selection: \n  1. Legendre: Orthogonal on [0,2] \n  2. Trigonometric: Handles periodicity \n  3. Truncated Gaussian: Smooth decay\n\n- Initial condition: \n  - Use parent solution projected\n  - Gaussian random projection \n  - Line search maxima detection\n\n- Optimization schedule:\n  - Learning rate: 10\u207b\u2074 (annealed)\n  - Barrier parameter: Initial 1, final 10\u2077\n\n- Problem size:\n  - Start p=8 (basis terms)\n  - Increase p to 16 if underconstrained\n  - Decrease to 4 if overconstrained\n\n- Dimensionality issues:\n  - QR factorization to reduce redundant dimensions\n  - PCA to detect useless modes\n\nCompute budget and robustness\n- Time estimation:\n  - Forward map: O(p n)\n  - Backward map: O(p)\n  - Barrier complexity: O(p\u00b2)\n\n- Gradient computation:\n  - Automatic differentiation:\n    h = \u03a3x_k \u03c6_k + \u03bc\n    (dh/d\u03b8) = [\u03c6_k, 0] (partial derivatives)\n\n- Memory: (p+1)\u207a coefficients with up to 10\u00b3 evaluations\n\n- Stalling detection:\n  - Gradient descent stagnation: max change < 1e\u207b\u2074\n  - Twice longer than usual convergence\n  - Fallback to basis expansion\n\n- Fallback procedure:\n  - If optimizer fails: Increase basis dimensions\n  - If integral constraint violated: Project coefficients\n  - If barrier failed: Reduce basis and restart\n\nValidation and return contract\n1. Feasibility:\n- Integral constraint: 1-e\u207b\u00b3\n- Inequality: max|\u03bc - \u03a3c_k| < 1e\u207b\u2076\n- Variable bounds: Integral projection\n\n2. Objective:\n- Compute C_5 exactly: max_k \u222bh(x)[1-h(x+k)]dx\n- Using: np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode='full') * dx\n\n3. Output format:\nfinal_h = \u03b8-projection to n=10\u2074 points\nC_5_value = exact integrated max\n\n4. Sanity checks:\n- Sum(h) must be 1/2\n- Elements: 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1\n- Not nan, not inf\n\nThe continuous basis approach ensures global exploration, while constraints are maintained by projection and barrier methods. This extends beyond discrete solutions by leveraging continuous optimization theory and greedy expansion capabilities.",
